  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "This is the easy version of TOOFAR, and is worth 404040 points.\n\nAn array AAA of length MMM is said to be prefix-balanced under the following conditions:\n\n\nLet SAS_ASA​ denote the set of all elements that appear in AAA.\nFor each x∈SAx \\in S_Ax∈SA​, and index iii (1≤i≤M1 \\leq i \\leq M1≤i≤M), let fi(x)f_i(x)fi​(x) denote the number of times xxx appears among [A1,A2,…,Ai][A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_i][A1​,A2​,…,Ai​].\n\nThat is, fi(x)f_i(x)fi​(x) denotes the frequency of xxx in AAA's prefix of length iii.\nThen, AAA is called prefix-balanced if, for **every** triple of integers (x,y,i)(x, y, i)(x,y,i) such that x,y∈SAx, y \\in S_Ax,y∈SA​ and 1≤i≤M1 \\leq i \\leq M1≤i≤M, we have\n\n∣fi(x)−fi(y)∣≤1|f_i(x) - f_i(y)| \\leq 1∣fi​(x)−fi​(y)∣≤1\nFor example, the arrays [1,2,1][1, 2, 1][1,2,1] and [1,3,2,3][1, 3, 2, 3][1,3,2,3] are prefix-balanced, but [2,3,2,4][2, 3, 2, 4][2,3,2,4] is not (the prefix of length 333 contains two occurrences of 222 and no occurrences of 444).\n\nYou are given two integers NNN and MMM.\n\nThere are MNM^NMN arrays of length NNN whose elements lie between 111 and MMM. How many of them are prefix-balanced?\n\nThe answer might be large, so find it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of a single line of input, containing two space-separated integers NNN and MMM.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of arrays of prefix-balanced arrays of length NNN, whose elements lie in [1,M][1, M][1,M]. Report the answer modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤5⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 5\\cdot 10^51≤N≤5⋅105",
      "1≤M≤5⋅1051 \\leq M \\leq 5\\cdot 10^51≤M≤5⋅105",
      "The sum of NNN and the sum of MMM over all test cases both won't exceed 5⋅1055\\cdot 10^55⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n1 10\n3 4\n5 8\n3 4567",
        "output": "10\n52\n15688\n402085806",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: There are 101010 possible arrays, all of which are prefix-balanced.\nTest case 222: There are 43=644^3 = 6443=64 possible arrays. Of them, the ones that are not prefix-balanced are:\n[1,1,2],[1,1,3],[1,1,4],[1, 1, 2], [1, 1, 3], [1, 1, 4],[1,1,2],[1,1,3],[1,1,4],\n[2,2,1],[2,2,3],[2,2,4],[2, 2, 1], [2, 2, 3], [2, 2, 4],[2,2,1],[2,2,3],[2,2,4],\n[3,3,1],[3,3,2],[3,3,4],[3, 3, 1], [3, 3, 2], [3, 3, 4],[3,3,1],[3,3,2],[3,3,4],\n[4,4,1],[4,4,2],[4,4,3].[4, 4, 1], [4, 4, 2], [4, 4, 3].[4,4,1],[4,4,2],[4,4,3].\nTest case 444: The actual answer is 952352993419523529934195235299341, which when taken modulo 998244353998244353998244353 is 402085806402085806402085806."
      }
